// codebox_mrg.gen -- f_vf_lbm: the obstacle mask, folded into the third state plane. 192x108 float32.
// Mirror: the mask step of the bench test (luma of the mask above 0.5, edge columns never obstacle).
//
// Inlets: first = the third state plane from the hold stage (hot: it triggers this render; R = population 8),
// second = the obstacle mask at render resolution (cold, from the module inlet).
// Output: R = population 8 unchanged, G = obstacle flag (1 inside the obstacle), B and A = 0. The collide stage reads
// the flag from G of its third inlet. Keeping the mask here (not in collide) leaves collide at three inlets, the
// most the codebox bench can drive.
//   - MASK: luma (0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B) averaged over a 4 x 4 grid of nearest taps across this texel's
//     footprint: exact at 1:1, a box filter when the mask is larger. Obstacle where the average is above 0.5.
//   - the first and last columns are never obstacle (the inflow and outflow edges; T014 default: shield them)
//   - an unconnected mask inlet reads black, so no obstacle
W = 192;
H = 108;
px = floor(norm.x * W);
py = floor(norm.y * H);
cu = (px + 0.5) / W;
cv = (py + 0.5) / H;
is_in = switch(px < 0.5, 1, 0);
is_out = switch(px > W - 1.5, 1, 0);

msum = 0;
for (ta = 0; ta < 4; ta += 1) {
  ox = ((ta + 0.5) / 4 - 0.5) / W;
  for (tb = 0; tb < 4; tb += 1) {
    oy = ((tb + 0.5) / 4 - 0.5) / H;
    msum += nearest(in2, vec(cu + ox, cv + oy)).x * 0.299 + nearest(in2, vec(cu + ox, cv + oy)).y * 0.587 + nearest(in2, vec(cu + ox, cv + oy)).z * 0.114;
  }
}
m = switch(msum / 16 > 0.5, 1, 0) * (1 - is_in) * (1 - is_out);

out1 = vec(nearest(in1, vec(cu, cv)).x, m, 0, 0);
